Package: hifiberry-jellyfin
Architecture: all
# Extension metadata. These XB- fields are the ONLY thing the WebUI's
# extension catalog reads (configurator's extensions/catalog.py builds every
# card from the apt record) -- omit one and it silently falls back: no
# Extension-Name shows the raw package name, no Extension-Category files a
# player under "Tools". dpkg strips the XB- prefix in the built record.
XB-Hifiberry-Extension: yes
XB-Extension-Name: Jellyfin
XB-Extension-Category: player
# postinst adds the player user to the render group (video decoding and
# display) when it is not a member yet, and only then asks for a reboot.
XB-Extension-Needs-Reboot: maybe
# Served by hifiberry-webui itself, so this resolves on a device with no
# internet access; an external URL would leave a broken image offline. The
# WebUI has no Jellyfin icon, so its generic screen icon stands in. The
# package's own icon (players.d/icons/jellyfin.svg) is served by
# config-server only once the package is installed, too late for the
# catalog.
XB-Extension-Icon-Url: /images/svg/tv.svg
# curl and alsa-utils: the hardware volume script (hifiberry-volume.lua)
# asks config-server for the volume control and drives it with amixer.
# hifiberry-configurator 2.19.0 is the first with the "text" setting type
# the server address uses; hifiberry-webui 0.28.0 the first that shows it,
# and the first with the player card's Quick Connect sign-in.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${venv:Python},
 python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, python3-pil, libmpv2,
 curl, alsa-utils,
 hifiberry-configurator (>= 2.19.0), hifiberry-audiocontrol,
 hifiberry-webui (>= 0.28.0)
Description: Jellyfin cast target for HiFiBerryOS
 Makes the device a playback target for Jellyfin: cast music, movies and
 series to it from any Jellyfin app. Audio plays through the normal
 HiFiBerryOS audio path; video plays full-screen on HDMI when a display is
 connected.
 .
 Runs jellyfin-mpv-shim, which is included in this package together with
 the Python libraries it needs.
